    "created_at": "2016-10-04T01:30:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-04T01:30:29Z",
    "body": "@mikewest So I'd like to make a concrete proposal, because shipping noopener in Firefox is currently blocked on this being resolved, unless we were to just make something up and ship it...\n1. We take the changes from this pull request, so that noopener never reuses an existing named browsing context.\n2. Noopener is ignored when targeting `_self`, `_top`, or `_parent`, so that it does not disown the opener in that case.\n3. Possibly add verbiage to the effect that noopener is ignored when it ends up targeting an existing browsing context (e.g. if the UA diverts the window.open into an existing tab).  Because really, it only makes sense to do the disowning thing if we in fact created a new browsing context...\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
